// Local sibling development. Copy to go.work to edit GoSX or Arbiter next to
// the Studio:
//
//     cp go.work.example go.work
//
// go.work is gitignored on purpose. It overrides the pinned versions in
// go.mod for your working tree only, so your local edits never decide what
// CI, a release, or another developer builds.
//
// This replaces the `replace m31labs.dev/gosx => ../gosx` directive go.mod
// used to carry. That directive switched off version resolution for everyone:
// the build read whatever the sibling folder happened to hold, with no
// version and no checksum, so `require m31labs.dev/gosx v0.29.5` was inert
// while the tree actually built against something months newer. A sibling
// deleting a package Studio used broke the build with nothing to point at.
//
// go.mod now pins real versions that go.sum checksums. To move to a newer
// GoSX, publish the tag and bump go.mod — deliberately, in a commit that
// shows the suite still passes.
go 1.26

use .

replace m31labs.dev/gosx => ../gosx

replace m31labs.dev/arbiter => ../arbiter
